.TH DEVNODES 1M "31 October 2026" "amix-base"
.SH NAME
devnodes \- re-create missing device nodes at boot
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /etc/init.d/devnodes start
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B devnodes
runs at every boot as
.BR /etc/rc2.d/S20devnodes ,
after the file systems are mounted and before the devices are used.
It makes again each device node that a package installed and that is no
longer there.
.PP
The nodes that should exist are the character and block special files
under
.B /dev
that the installed packages list in
.BR /var/sadm/install/contents :
every driver package ships its nodes as package objects.
A missing node is made with the minor number, mode, owner and group of its
record, and with this major number:
.TP
.I a stock node
(class
.BR none )
the major number of its record.
.TP
.I a module's node
(its class is the name of the kernel module that drives it)
the major number the running kernel's registry gives that module, as
.B kbootset major
prints it.
A node that is there at another major number is made again, and a record
that disagrees with the registry is reported as a packaging error.
When the registry does not know the module, the record's major is used.
.PP
A stock node that is there but differs from its record is left as it is,
and reported.
Nodes made outside the packages, such as the disk nodes
.B kbootset nodes
makes and
.BR /dev/kinfo ,
are not looked at.
.PP
Each node made and each one left is written to
.BR /var/adm/rc.log ,
with a count at the end; a boot with nothing to do writes nothing.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /var/sadm/install/contents
the installed objects, and with them the nodes.
.TP
.B /var/adm/rc.log
what was made.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rc.subr (1M),
.BR kbootset (1M)
